					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-645478#post-1803407</guid>
				<title>Testing everything for everything</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-645478/nacho-business#post-1803407</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 24 Jun 2013 17:55:02 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>toadking07</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1632267</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The list for testing SCPs must be huge, as brought up in here. The idea that these items could cause any number of insane happenings just by talking politely to them, or by wearing them, or by putting them close to a human/dog/cat/dolphin/whale/<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">unicorn</span>, I mean, you could have something in containment for years thinking it just turned blood into tomato paste and then find out during a breach that if it doesn't touch human flesh for over a year it starts generating ketchup on its own.</p> <p>For some in containment I can't see testing ever stopping.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
